good in terms of a kind of moral  sensitivity to the problems of ghettos  over the years by the way the book  publishers have to pay these guys to  never sit no Henry Hampton says this  beautifully written thought-provoking  and at times controversial work deserves  a wide readership who is Henry Hampton  eyes on the prize did you see that he's  the guy who did eyes on the prize he's a  great documentary film producer he did  eyes on the prize he did eyes on the  prize part two he's now working on  two other very ambitious projects one a  history of the Great Depression and one  history the war on poverty what's next  for Nicholas lemon  I don't know I'm back working at the  Atlantic and and I'm not going to sort  of push to get another book out real  soon I take a long time to do these  things and I imagine it will be several  more years before I've got I definitely  want to do another book and I want it to  be about as I said vaguely American life  but I don't know exactly what and and my  job doing my job for the Atlantic is a  great way to do R&amp;D and look around and  see what's out there to write about so  that's what I'm doing now this is the  book the promised land the great black  migration and how it changed America  Nicholas lemon the author thank you very  much thank you
 

